{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PnAJWh67YvskLym7x7NnxB","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Gauntletdown\n18:## Contents\n36:## 0. Read this first\n50:## 1. The game on one page\n59:### What makes Gauntlet distinctive, and how this game captures it\n76:### Originality guardrails (non-negotiable)\n85:## 2. Deliverables and folder layout\n87:### The run folder (this folder)\n96:### The dev subfolder\n120:### What the finished demo contains\n126:## 3. Architecture\n128:### 3.1 Base\n134:### 3.2 Modules (`game/src/`, concatenated in name order inside one IIFE)\n171:### 3.3 Runtime model: simulation, intents, view, network\n192:### 3.4 Scenes and flow\n205:### 3.5 Engine changes (the engine is ours to change; keep each one small and tested)\n222:### 3.6 Build and bundle (`build.mjs`)\n253:## 4. Systems and mechanics (the spec)\n257:### 4.1 Floors, the map and the legend\n291:### 4.2 Heroes\n319:### 4.3 Controls and prompts (10-foot, controller-first)\n343:### 4.4 Combat and damage\n351:### 4.5 Monsters\n372:### 4.6 Generators\n379:### 4.7 Items\n404:### 4.8 Level features\n422:### 4.9 Floor flow\n430:### 4.10 Death, rising again, continue, game over, high scores\n437:### 4.11 Scoring\n441:### 4.12 The narrator: \"The Gaunt\"\n448:### 4.13 Camera and local co-op\n458:### 4.14 HUD (canvas pixel art, anchored to `r.W`/`r.H`, clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n468:### 4.15 Front-end screens (canvas pixel art; big; mouse, keys and controller)\n479:### 4.16 Pause menu and Settings\n484:### 4.17 Dev Tools (from the pause menu; not in sessions, not in attract)\n495:### 4.18 Attract mode and the autopilot\n503:### 4.19 Touch-only devices\n510:### 4.20 Online: AI Hub sessions (shared world) and the game on its own\n548:### 4.21 Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n582:### 4.22 Art direction\n608:### 4.23 Animation\n627:### 4.24 Difficulty, scaling and the tuning table\n654:## 5. Content\n656:### 5.1 Story and story beats\n671:### 5.2 Heroes\n675:### 5.3 Bestiary\n686:### 5.4 Items\n690:### 5.5 Floors\n697:########################################\n698:#@@......#..........#..........#.......#\n699:#@@......#...g......#....$.....#...*...#\n700:#........#..........#..........#.......#\n701:#...b....#..######..#...g......#...h...#\n702:#........#..#.k..#..#..........+.......#\n703:#............g...#.......f.....+...E...#\n704:#........#..#....#..#..........#.......#\n705:#........#..######..#....G.....#...$...#\n706:#........#..........#..........#.......#\n707:####..########..#########..#############\n708:#......................#...............#\n709:#..g......##....G......#.....g.........#\n710:#..........#...........#.........*.....#\n711:#....f.....#....g...........######.....#\n712:#..........#................#..........#\n713:#..$.......####.......$.....#...f......#\n714:#...........................#..........#\n715:#.........g.................#....b.....#\n716:########################################\n738:### 5.6 Narrator lines (the Gaunt)\n802:### 5.7 How to Play cards\n813:### 5.8 About and Credits (paged)\n825:## 6. Build order and milestones\n849:## 7. Riskiest parts and how to de-risk them\n867:## 8. Testing\n869:### 8.1 The one command\n873:### 8.2 Harness for headless suites\n879:### 8.3 Floors suite\n883:### 8.4 Sim suite (headless, per system)\n899:### 8.5 Play suite (the scripted playthrough of the whole game)\n906:### 8.6 Net suite (Node) and hub suite (browser)\n917:### 8.7 UI suite (browser) and screenshots\n925:## 9. Done checklist (every TASK.md requirement, and where it is met)\n954:## Appendix A: `exit-interview.json` prefill\n997:## Appendix B: Source Information draft (finish it with your own facts)\n1014:## Appendix C: Engine and hub facts this plan relies on (verified while planning)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"24682cce-b194-4350-9438-db4b975b747a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:34.695Z","too