{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrZeJRkaxTWDQcaLVEt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FTuG9ozKeXfoxaXViKG9kH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build--20261104-050250--x8ffc89-work/04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db/tool-results/bl5ye5sy8.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":973,"cache_read_input_tokens":46062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":973},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"9f3e0715-d0bc-4255-a7f4-e6c23989e1bb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:38.781Z","request_id":"req_011CghrZe24JqTQuAci54udM","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FTuG9ozKeXfoxaXViKG9kH":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build--20261104-050250--x8ffc89-work/04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db/tool-results/bl5ye5sy8.txt"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FTuG9ozKeXfoxaXViKG9kH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## 1. The game on one page\n2\t\n3\t**Core loop (one sentence, as the engine's guide asks):** descend floor by floor through a starving dungeon, blasting hordes and the generators that breed them, grabbing keys, food and treasure before your ever-draining life force runs out: together, and racing each other for score.\n4\t\n5\t**Genre:** arcade co-op dungeon crawler: a top-down hack-and-shoot (\"hack-and-slash shooter\") with maze exploration. Catalogue genre: **Action**.\n6\t**Perspective:** **three-quarter overhead** (the engine's `threequarter` view, 55° pitch): it shows wall faces and character faces (the N64-era *Gauntlet Legends* angle) while keeping the maze readable. **Top-down** (`topdown`, 80°) and **isometric** (`iso`) are selectable in Settings. The rules are the same in every view.\n7\t**Players:** 1–4. Couch co-op with drop-in and drop-out (gamepads, and up to two players on one keyboard); online 1–4 through AI Hub sessions.\n8\t**Session length:** a full descent is about 35–50 minutes (9 floors, 2 treasure rooms, a boss); an AI Hub round is 6 minutes.\n9\t\n10\t### What makes Gauntlet distinctive, and how this game captures it\n11\t\n12\t| Source trait | In Gauntletdown |\n13\t|---|---|\n14\t| Four archetype heroes with clearly different stats, up to four at once | Berserker, Shieldmaiden, Ranger, Hexer (original characters), each with its own armor, shot, melee, magic and speed; 1–4 players |\n15\t| Health ticks down every second; food is life | **Life force** drains 1 per second; roasts, loaves and cider restore it; health is shown as a big number, like the arcade |\n16\t| Endless hordes from generators | Six generator types breed monsters until destroyed; crowds jam corridors |\n17\t| Monsters come in strength levels and weaken when hit | Ranks 3, 2, 1: a wounded rank-3 monster visibly shrinks to rank 2, then 1 |\n18\t| Keys open doors; magic potions clear the screen | A key opens a whole run of doors; a **Blast Flask** strikes every monster on screen |\n19\t| \"Don't shoot the food\"; shooting a potion wastes it | Cider and stew can be shot (and are destroyed); a shot flask detonates at half power |\n20\t| Death: can't be shot, drains your health, only magic kills it | **The Tithe**, a reaper that drains up to 200 and only magic can kill |\n21\t| The booming announcer (\"... needs food badly\", \"... shot the food\") | **The Gaunt**, the dungeon's own voice: terse booming callouts in the same style, with original lines, spoken in deep gibberish under big captions |\n22\t| Exits, skip-exits, traps, transporters, treasure rooms, stun tiles, force fields | All present (4.8) |\n23\t| Co-op that is also competitive | Individual scores; whoever takes the stairs gets the exit bonus; AI Hub standings are by score |\n24\t| Insert-a-coin drop-in, a loop that never ends | Join any time; fallen heroes **rise again**; after the ending, **Descent II** loops the dungeon harder |\n25\t| Walls turn into exits if you dawdle | The Gaunt grows impatient: doors open at 3:00, every wall becomes a stair at 4:00 |\n26\t\n27\t### Originality guardrails (non-negotiable)\n28\t\n29\tBuild an original game *in the genre* of Gauntlet, not a recreation of it (TASK.md and the system rules):\n30\t- No names, characters, art, music, levels or exact lines from any Gauntlet game. Not Thor, Thyra, Merlin or Questor; not \"Warrior/Valkyrie/Wizard/Elf\" as the class set; not \"Wizard needs food, badly\", \"Elf shot the food\", \"Remember, don't shoot food\", or \"Shots do not hurt other players... yet\". The lines in 5.6 are original and follow the source's *style*: short, booming, third-person, darkly funny.\n31\t- All floors are this plan's own layouts. All music is original composition. Monster designs are this plan's (hunger-themed: ghosts with gaping mouths, kitchen imps, frying-pan friars).\n32\t- The title is a riff on the source's name, as TASK.md requires.\n33\t\n34\t---\n35\t\n36\t## 2. Deliverables and folder layout\n37\t\n38\t### The run folder (this folder)\n39\t\n40\t```\n41\tPLAN.md, STAGE.md, TASK.md                              (given)\n42\tGauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174804.html   <- the game, one file, works from file://\n43\texit-interview.json                                      <- written last (Appendix A), must parse as JSON\n44\tGauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174804/      <- every dev file\n45\t```\n46\t\n47\t### The dev subfolder\n48\t\n49\tStart it as a copy of the engine's `dist/handoff/` (sparse-clone it: `git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git` then `git sparse-checkout set dist/handoff`, and copy `dist/handoff/*` into the dev subfolder), so the engine's tools work with their own paths. Then add:\n50\t\n51\t```\n52\t<dev>/\n53\t  my-3d2dge.js          the full engine (every module included), PATCHED as listed in 3.5\n54\t  ENGINE-CHANGES.md     each engine change: what, why, its test (feeds Engine Feedback)\n55\t  API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, docs/, tools/, src/assets/ (from the handoff: references, tools, the asset store)\n56\t  package.json          from the handoff (pins Playwright 1.63.0); `npm install` once\n57\t  hub/                  session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md, fetched with\n58\t                        curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/<file>\n59\t  game/\n60\t    src/NN-*.js         the game's source fragments (3.2), concatenated in name order into one IIFE\n61\t    game.js             built from src/ (never edited by hand)\n62\t    index.html          the dev page: session.js first in <head>, then my-3d2dge.js, then game.js\n63\t  build.mjs             builds game/game.js and the single-file deliverable (3.6)\n64\t  tests/                run.mjs (the one command) and the suites (section 8)\n65\t  docs/DESIGNER.md      how to add a floor, a monster, an item or a line (the \"designer tools\" note)\n66\t  shots/                screenshots for look review (not shipped)\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tThe handoff's template game goes: `game/game.js` is overwritten by `build.mjs`, and `game/test.mjs` (and `kits/`, once you have taken what you need) can be deleted. The deliverable is only the single HTML file; the dev folder is the workshop.\n70\t\n71\t### What the finished demo contains\n72\t\n73\tTitle screen with attract mode; main menu; class select; How to Play; High Scores; About/Credits (with the four feedback sections); 9 floors in three realms, 2 treasure rooms and a boss; an ending, credits and the Descent II loop; game over, continue and initials entry; the engine's pause menu, settings and controls (adjusted), plus **Dev Tools**; local co-op 1–4; AI Hub shared-world sessions 1–4; the touch-only notice. Audio entirely synthesized in code.\n74\t\n75\t---\n76\t\n77\t## 4. Systems and mechanics (the spec)\n78\t\n79\tAll distances are world units (one tile = 16). Speeds are units per second. Every number marked † is a `TUNE` entry (4.24) and a Dev slider.\n80\t\n81\t### 4.1 Floors, the map and the legend\n82\t\n83\t- A floor is a `def('floors', id, { name, realm, no, music, par, rank, genRank, specials: [], amulets: [], intro: [...], next, rows: [...] })`. `rows` are ASCII strings, all the same width, bordered by walls. The parser builds an `E.TileMap` (wall types per realm, `cut: true, cutH: 6` so walls in front of the camera drop low; `ao: 6`), the entity lists, door groups, trap groups, transporter pairs and beams.\n84\t- **Wall height 24**, a little below a hero's head. Hero shots fly at z 12, so they pass over the banquet table (h 10) and are stopped by walls (the engine's `Bullets` already compare `map.heightAt` with the bullet's z).\n85\t- Corridors are at least 2 tiles wide; rooms 6–14 tiles across. Floors range from 40×20 (the tutorial) to 64×44.\n86\t\n87\t**The legend (shared by every floor):**\n88\t\n89\t| Char | Meaning | Char | Meaning |\n90\t|---|---|---|---|\n91\t| `#` | wall (realm stone) | `@` | hero start (author 4; fewer are padded on free neighbours) |\n92\t| `%` | accent wall (shelves, bone wall, iron) | `E` | stairs down (exit) |\n93\t| `X` | cracked wall (4 HP, shots break it) | `2`–`9` | skip stairs to floor N |\n94\t| `+` | door (iron bars); 4-connected runs open together | `O` | transporter pad (paired in reading order: 1st↔2nd, 3rd↔4th) |\n95\t| `T` | trap wall, removed when any `^` plate is stepped on | `!` | stun rune |\n96\t| `Y` | trap wall, removed when any `v` plate is stepped on | `s` | spikes (cycling) |\n97\t| `?` | fake wall: drawn as a wall, walkable (a secret) | `\\|` `-` | force-field beam, vertical / horizontal (pylons drawn where it meets walls) |\n98\t| `~` | lava or chasm (blocked floor, glows in the Furnace) | `^` `v` | pressure plates |\n99\t| `.` | floor | `,` | floor variant (rug, dirt, bone dust) |\n100\t| `k` | key | `f` | roast (+100, can't be shot) |\n101\t| `b` | loaf (+50, can't be shot) | `j` | cider jug (+100, shootable) |\n102\t| `z` | spoiled stew (poison, shootable) | `m` | Blast Flask (magic) |\n103\t| `u` | special potion (type from `meta.specials`, reading order) | `a` | amulet (type from `meta.amulets`, reading order) |\n104\t| `$` | gold | `*` | gem |\n105\t| `h` | chest | `l` | locked chest (needs a key) |\n106\t| `w` | crown | `B` | Dinner Bell |\n107\t| `g` `n` `o` `i` `y` `x` `t` | monsters: hungerghost, gnasher, pot-lobber, cinder imp, fryar, snatcher, the Tithe (rank from `meta.rank`) | `G` `N` `L` `I` `F` `S` | generators: ash urn, gnasher den, crockery hutch, ember grate, candle shrine, sack heap (rank from `meta.genRank`) |\n108\t| `K` | King Famish (boss floor) | `=` | banquet table (low wall, h 10) |\n109\t| `P` | a table cell carrying a feast platter (+200, shootable) | `U` | a table cell carrying a soup tureen (the boss floor's ghost generator) |\n110\t\n111\tPer-cell overrides go in `meta.ranks: { 'x,y': 3 }`, set pieces in `meta.props: [[shapeId, cx, cy, facing]]`, snatcher escape points and boss spawn points in `meta.points`.\n112\t\n113\t- **Automatic decoration:** a deterministic pass (`E.hash2(cx, cy)`) puts a torch (`r.prop('torch', ..., { light: true })`) on about one wall face in six along open floor, and 3–8 realm props per room against walls (Larder: barrels, kegs, sacks, crates, hanging hams; Ossuary: skulls, bones, coffins, candelabras, cobwebs, urns; Furnace: braziers, fire drums, anvils, chains). Decoration goes only on empty floor cells beside walls (never on an item, monster, generator, plate, pad, rune, beam, spike or stairs cell). Props that block are made solid with `map.solid`, and the validator re-runs the solvability check (8.3) with them in place, so decoration can never cut a floor in two.\n114\t\n115\t### 4.2 Heroes\n116\t\n117\t| | **Berserker** | **Shieldmaiden** | **Ranger** | **Hexer** |\n118\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n119\t| Character | Brakka Ironbelly | Hilde Stoutheart | Fenn Quickfletch | Old Mother Wix |\n120\t| Look | Humanoid `bulky` size 1.15, `weapon: 'axe'`, `hat: 'horned'`, fur cape, bare arms; red and brown | `heroic` 1.1, `weapon: 'sword'`, `offhand: 'shield'`, `hat: 'helmet'`, `hair: 'ponytail'`; blue and steel | `heroic` 1.05, `weapon: 'bow'`, hood, short cape, `sleeves: 'long'`; green and leather | `chibi` 1.05, `weapon: 'staff'`, `hat: 'pointed'`, `outfit: 'robe'`, `hunch: .3`, `face: { eyes: 'big' }`; yellow and purple |\n121\t| Hub seat (colour) | 1 (red `#e8443a`) | 2 (blue `#3b82f6`) | 3 (green `#22c55e`) | 4 (yellow `#f5b700`) |\n122\t| Move speed | 62 | 66 | 78 | 64 |\n123\t| Armor (damage taken ×) | 0.75 | 0.60 | 0.90 | 1.00 |\n124\t| Shot | spinning hand-axe | javelin | arrow | hex-bolt |\n125\t| Shot damage | 3, pierces 1 foe | 2 | 1 | 2, plus 1 splash within 12 |\n126\t| Shot speed / cooldown | 190 / 0.34 s | 240 / 0.27 s | 300 / 0.15 s | 220 / 0.26 s |\n127\t| Melee damage per swing | 5 | 4 | 2 | 1.5 |\n128\t| Melee moves (`E.MOVES`) | `overhead` → `spin` | `thrust` → `bash` (shield) | `jab` → `cross` (dagger) | `bash` (staff) |\n129\t| Magic power (monsters / generators) | 1.0 / 1.0 | 1.4 / 1.0 | 1.7 / 1.0 | 2.5 / 2.0 |\n130\t| Throw animation | `throw` | `throw` | bow draw (new spec, 4.23) | `cast` |\n131\t| Voice | low, gruff | firm, mid | quick, light | high, cackling |\n132\t\n133\t- **Health (life force):** starts at 700†, no maximum (numbers above 9999 show as 9999+). Drains 1 per second† for every living hero, all the time on a floor (not on cards or menus).\n134\t- **Shooting:** fire is held for auto-fire at the class's cooldown. The shot leaves the weapon hand (`rig.hand('R')`, or 8 ahead at z 12) in the aim direction; range 220 (its `life` is range ÷ speed). Shots are `E.Bullets` on the ground plane, `team: 'hero'`, `data: { owner, kind }`. They pass through allies (but see ally stun below).\n135\t- **Smart melee:** when fire is pressed and a non-ghost monster is within reach (hero r + monster r + 8) inside ±50° of the aim, the hero swings its melee combo (`E.Combo`) instead of throwing. Melee hits everything in the arc (`attack.hits` with `E.inArc(hero, aim, m, 22, 1.2)`), with `game.hitFx`. Hungerghosts can't be struck: up close the hero throws point-blank instead.\n136\t- **Plant:** holding Plant (Shift, L2) stops the hero, which turns with the movement input and keeps firing: the arcade \"stand and shoot\" stance. **Keyboard-only firing** (fire from a key while mouse aim is off, below) plants automatically, as in the arcade.\n137\t- **Aim:** right stick: its direction through `game.view.screenDirToGround` (pushing it past 0.5 also fires, a setting); mouse: toward the ground point under the cursor (`game.mouseGround()`), with a reticle, while `input.aimSource === 'mouse'` and the mouse moved in the last 3 s or a mouse button is firing (the engine's `aimSource` only changes on mouse or pad input, never on keys, so a stale cursor must not keep aiming); otherwise the hero's facing (the last movement direction). **Aim assist** (Off / Low 8° / High 16°): snaps to the nearest visible monster or generator within that cone and 200 units.\n138\t- **Magic (Blast Flask):** pressing Magic with at least one flask uses it: every monster inside the user's screen rectangle (the shared screen in local co-op; the user's own view in a session) takes `4 × magic power` damage (rounded up); generators there take `2 × magic-vs-generators`; the Tithe dies. A white flash, a shockwave ring, a choir sting, the hero's `cast` pose.\n139\t- **Carry limits:** 9 keys and 9 flasks (12 with Deep Pockets). Pickups over the limit stay on the floor.\n140\t- **Ally stun:** from floor 6 on (and in Descent II), a hero shot that touches an ally stuns that ally for 0.35 s (Settings: Ally stun On/Off; default On). The narrator announces it at floor 6's start.\n141\t- **Starving look:** below 200 health the rig hunches (`hunch` rises with hunger), the walk slows its bob, and a heartbeat plays for local players.\n142\t\n143\t### 4.3 Controls and prompts (10-foot, controller-first)\n144\t\n145\tThe game is designed around a PS5 DualSense in the browser's standard mapping, played on a TV; keyboard and mouse get the keys PC players expect for a twin-stick shooter, on the same screens. Custom input preset `GD_INPUT` (the engine's menu actions are added by the engine):\n146\t\n147\t| Action | Keyboard and mouse (player 1) | DualSense | Xbox labels (setting) |\n148\t|---|---|---|---|\n149\t| Move | W A S D (and arrows when alone on the keyboard) | Left stick, D-pad | Left stick, D-pad |\n150\t| Aim | Mouse | Right stick | Right stick |\n151\t| Fire (hold) | Left click, Space, J | R2, ✕ | RT, A |\n152\t| Magic | Right click, Q, K | △, R1 | Y, RB |\n153\t| Plant (hold) | Shift | L2 | LT |\n154\t| Change camera view | V | (Settings) | (Settings) |\n155\t| Zoom | Wheel, - and = | (Settings) | (Settings) |\n156\t| Pause and menu | Esc, P | Options | Menu |\n157\t| Menus | arrows / mouse hover and click, Enter, Esc or Backspace | D-pad/stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | A confirm, B back |\n158\t| Join (local) | 2 (the keyboard's right half) | Options on a free controller | Menu on a free controller |\n159\t\n160\t- In `GD_INPUT`, list each action's gamepad codes with the prompt you want first (Fire: `Pad7` before `Pad0`, so prompts say R2; Magic: `Pad3` before `Pad5`, so they say △), since a prompt shows an action's first code for the device.\n161\t- A second keyboard player (who joined with 2) gets the right half, as the engine splits it: arrows to move, then `.` `/` `,` for Fire, Magic, Plant (and the numpad). Player 1 keeps W A S D with F G H for the same three, plus the mouse.\n162\t- **Create (Share) does nothing**: in sessions the hub owns Create + Options (engine change E4).\n163\t- **Prompts follow the device used last** (`input.label(action)`): PlayStation glyphs for any controller by default (✕ ○ □ △, L1/R1/L2/R2, Options), Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB/RB/LT/RT, Menu) with Settings → Button symbols, key names and \"Left click\"/\"Right click\" for keyboard and mouse. Never hard-code a key in text: every prompt, card and help page is built from `label()`. Each local player's panel shows that player's own prompts.\n164\t- **The mouse in menus:** hover moves the focus, a click picks (E.Menu does this; class cards and How to Play pages must too). **The mouse in the world:** the reticle; hovering a monster or generator outlines it and shows its name and rank; clicking fires at it.\n165\t- **Touch:** no touch controls anywhere (4.19).\n166\t\n167\t### 4.4 Combat and damage\n168\t\n169\t- **Monster HP** is `baseHP × rank`; its **rank** is `ceil(hp / baseHP)` after each hit. When the rank drops, the rig shrinks (scale 1.15 → 1.0 → 0.88) and its palette pales, with a puff: the arcade's \"level\" system made visible.\n170\t- **Hero damage taken** = monster damage × class armor × difficulty × Iron Brew. Hero hit: `hurt` flinch, a red flash on the panel, a small knockback, a pain bark (Babble), a 0.25 s grace before the same monster's contact damage can hit again.\n171\t- **Heroes and monsters block each other.** A hero can be boxed in by a horde, as in the arcade; fight out or use magic. Resolve circle overlaps every step with an `E.SpatialHash` (cell 32): monsters push each other apart softly; heroes are pushed out of monsters.\n172\t- **Kills:** score = monster points × the rank it spawned at; `game.hitFx` on every hit; a death effect per type (ghost: a wail and a puff; gnasher: a tumble, `pose: 'down'`, then a fade; imp: a small explosion; fryar: smoke; Tithe: a bone burst).\n173\t- **Hit feedback:** hit-stop 0.03–0.05 s on melee, shake on magic and generator deaths, damage numbers only on generators and the boss (hordes would drown the screen in numbers).\n174\t\n175\t### 4.5 Monsters\n176\t\n177\t| Monster | Char | Generator | HP / rank | Speed r1/r2/r3 | Attack | Damage r1/r2/r3 | Points / rank | Notes |\n178\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n179\t| **Hungerghost** | `g` | Ash Urn `G` | 2 | 40 / 46 / 52 | flies into a hero, then vanishes | 10 / 20 / 30 | 10 | Can't be struck in melee; floats over runes and spikes; paths around walls like everyone |\n180\t| **Gnasher** | `n` | Gnasher Den `N` | 2 | 34 / 38 / 42 | club swing: 0.32 s wind-up, reach 14, every 0.9 s | 6 / 8 / 10 | 10 | The horde; club raised high in the wind-up |\n181\t| **Pot-Lobber** | `o` | Crockery Hutch `L` | 2 | 30 / 34 / 38 (flees at 46) | lobs a crock over walls (`E.arc`, apex 40, range 130) every 2.2 / 1.9 / 1.6 s at the hero's position plus lead; a shadow marks the landing 0.6 s ahead | 8 / 10 / 12 splash within 12 | 15 | Keeps 70–110 away, flees inside 56; its crocks are `Bullets` with `grav` and break on landing |\n182\t| **Cinder Imp** | `i` | Ember Grate `I` | 3 | 36 / 40 / 44 | bite (reach 10); fireball (speed 110, only with sight, every 1.8 s, 0.35 s mouth glow first) | bite 6 / 8 / 10, fireball 8 / 10 / 12 | 20 | Fireballs destroy shootable food they hit |\n183\t| **Fryar** | `y` | Candle Shrine `F` | 3 | 36 / 40 / 44 | frying-pan smack, 0.3 s wind-up | 8 / 10 / 12 | 25 | Visible 2.0 s, invisible 1.4 s (can't be hit; shots pass through); reappears up to 48 closer along its path, with smoke |\n184\t| **Snatcher** | `x` | Sack Heap `S` | 3 (rank 1 only) | 72 | steals on touch: a flask, else a key, else the active amulet | none | 100, plus the item back | Then flees to its heap or the nearest `meta.points.escape`; escapes with the item unless killed (then drops it) |\n185\t| **The Tithe** | `t` | none (placed, or the impatience timer) | immune | 52 | drains while touching: 6 health per 0.1 s, at most 200 per hero | drain | 1000 × (1–5), drawn from `rng.sim` | Only magic kills it (a flask, or a shot flask's blast); shots clink off; vanishes when it has taken 200 from a hero (\"THE TITHE IS PAID\") |\n186\t| **Dinner Bell** | `B` | none | object | none | a hero who touches it rings it and is **ON THE MENU** | none | none | Every monster targets that hero for 12 s, or until they touch an ally, who is then on the menu (a co-op hot potato); one ring per floor |\n187\t| **King Famish** | `K` | boss | 400 × (1 + 0.5 × (players − 1)) | 30 | plates, stomp, eating, charge, fog (5.3) | 10–15 per attack; fog triples the drain | 10,000 | Three phases (5.3) |\n188\t\n189\t**AI (23-sim-monsters.js):**\n190\t- **Navigation:** one multi-source `FlowField` toward every living hero (E1), rebuilt when a hero changes cell; each monster steps along `flow.dir`. While the Bell marks a hero, a single-source field toward that hero is used instead. Snatchers fleeing and lobbers keeping their distance use their own fields (toward the escape point; away from the hero by climbing the distance gradient).\n191\t- **Activation:** monsters farther than 20 tiles from every hero stand still (they wait in the dark, as in the arcade).\n192\t- **Telegraphs:** every enemy attack winds up visibly (raised club, mouth glow, landing shadow, pan drawn back) for at least 0.3 s, longer than any hero swing, as the engine's animation guide asks.\n193\t- **Amulet reactions:** Veil: monsters lose track of that hero unless adjacent and wander. Stench: monsters flee from that hero within 64.\n194\t- **Hazards:** force fields hurt monsters too (lure hordes through them); spikes and lava don't affect ghosts.\n195\t\n196\t### 4.6 Generators\n197\t\n198\t- HP `4 × rank`† (Dev multiplier); they take shot, melee and magic damage, and lose a rank, with a damage state, every 4 HP. Spawn interval r1 3.0 s, r2 2.2 s, r3 1.5 s (× spawn interval multiplier†, ÷ (1 + 0.25 × (players − 1))). A generator spawns only when a hero is within 15 tiles, it has fewer than 8 living children, and the floor is under its monster cap† (140; 100 in sessions). New monsters emerge into a free neighbouring cell over 0.4 s (rising from the generator with dust) at the generator's current rank.\n199\t- Destroyed: debris, a crumble sound, 25 × rank points, and a 10% chance to drop a loaf.\n200\t- Generators are static circular obstacles (r 7) in the same overlap pass as bodies, not TileMap walls, so destroying one needs no map change; shots hit them through `shots.hit`.\n201\t- Art (4.22): Ash Urn (ghosts), Gnasher Den (gnashers), Crockery Hutch (lobbers), Ember Grate (imps, flat and glowing, shoot it from any side), Candle Shrine (fryars), Sack Heap (snatchers), Soup Tureen (the boss's ghosts). Each has three damage states (intact, cracked, crumbling) as shape params, and breathes (a slow scale pulse) while it spawns.\n202\t\n203\t### 4.7 Items\n204\t\n205\t| Item | Char | Effect | Shootable | Points |\n206\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n207\t| Key | `k` | +1 key (limit 9) | no | 0 |\n208\t| Roast | `f` | +100 health† | no | 10 |\n209\t| Loaf | `b` | +50 health | no | 5 |\n210\t| Cider jug | `j` | +100 health | yes: destroyed, and the narrator names the culprit | 10 |\n211\t| Spoiled stew | `z` | −50 health and Queasy (move × 0.6 for 4 s, green face) | yes: destroying it is good | 0 |\n212\t| Blast Flask | `m` | +1 flask (limit 9) | yes: detonates at half the shooter's magic power within 80 | 0 |\n213\t| Special potion | `u` | permanent upgrade for the rest of the game (below) | no | 250 |\n214\t| Amulet | `a` | a 20 s power (below) | no | 100 |\n215\t| Gold | `$` | | no | 100 |\n216\t| Gem | `*` | | no | 250 |\n217\t| Chest | `h` | opens on touch (lid tween, coins burst) | no | 500 |\n218\t| Locked chest | `l` | needs and uses a key; drops a flask, a roast or a key | no | 1000 |\n219\t| Crown | `w` | | no | 2500 |\n220\t| Feast platter | `P` | +200 health (reachable from beside the table); King Famish eats them | yes | 20 |\n221\t\n222\tPickups happen on touch (hero r + 4). Food shows a crunchy \"chomp\" (squash and stretch, crumbs, a rising +100).\n223\t\n224\t**Special potions** (once per hero per type; icons under the panel): **Iron Brew** (damage taken × 0.8), **Ogre Ale** (melee × 1.5), **Quickshot Tonic** (cooldown × 0.75, shot speed × 1.2), **Hardshot Draught** (shot damage +1), **Witchwater** (magic × 1.5), **Featherfoot Cordial** (speed × 1.12), **Deep Pockets** (limits +3).\n225\t\n226\t**Amulets** (20 s each, a ring timer on the panel and around the hero): **Veil** (monsters lose track of you; drawn half-transparent), **Ironskin** (no damage; drain continues; gold shimmer), **Stench** (monsters flee from you; green fumes), **Ricochet** (shots bounce off walls up to 3 times, E3), **Rending** (shots pierce every monster and deal +1).\n227\t\n228\t### 4.8 Level features\n229\t\n230\t| Feature | Behaviour |\n231\t|---|---|\n232\t| Doors `+` | A hero with a key who pushes into a door cell (within r + 3) opens the whole 4-connected run and uses one key. The bars rise over 0.4 s (`map.set(cx, cy, 0)` per cell, plus a bars sprite that slides up) |\n233\t| Cracked walls `X` | 4 HP; any hero shot (via `onWall`, E3) or melee damages them; they collapse into rubble floor with dust. Hide shortcuts and stashes |\n234\t| Fake walls `?` | Drawn exactly as walls; walkable; shimmer when touched; the first one found triggers \"THAT WALL WAS LYING.\" |\n235\t| Trap plates `^` `v` | One-shot: stepping on any `^` removes every `T` wall (crumble, a rumble); `v` does the same for `Y`. Traps release hordes or reveal treasure |\n236\t| Transporters `O` | Stepping on a pad moves the hero to its pair with a swirl (0.6 s cooldown, 0.5 s invulnerable on arrival). Monsters don't use them |\n237\t| Stun runes `!` | Heroes stepping on one are stunned 0.8 s (can't move or fire), then immune to runes for 1.5 s |\n238\t| Force fields `\\|` `-` | Beams cycle 2 s on, 2 s off, flickering for 0.4 s before switching on. On: 12 damage and knockback to anything that touches (monsters too) |\n239\t| Spikes `s` | Cycle 1.6 s (0.5 s up, with a 0.25 s tremble before); 15 damage |\n240\t| Lava `~` | Blocked floor; glows (floor texels with glow, lights); heat shimmer under GPU lighting |\n241\t| Stairs `E` | Stand on the stairs for 1.0 s† (a ring fills around the hero; stepping off cancels) and **everyone** descends; the stair-taker gets the exit bonus |\n242\t| Skip stairs `2`–`9` | The same, to floor N (\"TOOK THE SHORT WAY DOWN\"); a carved number shows the target. Floors and treasure rooms in between are skipped; a realm card still plays when the skip enters a new realm |\n243\t| Impatience | At 150 s† \"THE GAUNT GROWS IMPATIENT\"; at 180 s† every door opens; at 240 s every wall becomes a stair (wall faces glow; pushing into any wall for 1 s descends). From floor 5, the Tithe arrives at 120 s† if none is on the floor |\n244\t| Treasure rooms | A 30 s† clock (big, top centre); treasure everywhere, no monsters, drain continues; the stairs are open. When the clock ends, \"THE HOARD SLAMS SHUT\" and everyone moves on. Taking every treasure: +2000 to whoever took the last |\n245\t\n246\t### 4.9 Floor flow\n247\t\n248\t1. **Floor card** (on entering): realm art behind, \"FLOOR 2\" big, the floor's name, the narrator's intro line (spoken), and for floors after the first, three numbers per player (score, kills, treasure). Continues on Fire/✕/Enter or after 5 s. In sessions the card is a 2 s banner and play never waits.\n249\t2. **Play** until the stairs. Heroes start on the `@` cells.\n250\t3. **Descent:** an iris transition (`game.go(..., { fade: 'iris', at: stairTaker })`), the heroes sink into the stairs, a descending arpeggio.\n251\t4. **Exit bonus** to the stair-taker: 500 + 5 per second under the floor's `par` (default 150 s).\n252\t5. **Realm cards** before floor 1, after each treasure room (entering realms II and III) and before floor 9: a short vignette (the party slides down a chute) and the realm's line (5.1).\n253\t\n254\t### 4.10 Death, rising again, continue, game over, high scores\n255\t\n256\t- **A hero falls** at 0 health: `pose: 'die'` (stagger, knees, topple), a ghostly wisp rises, \"BERSERKER HAS BEEN EATEN.\" Its panel shows **RISE: [Fire]**. Any time later, Fire brings it back beside a living ally with the starting health; the player's continues count goes up and their score is kept (the arcade's drop-in, without coins).\n257\t- **Everyone down:** \"CONTINUE? 10\" (`E.Arcade` continue countdown). Fire or Start from any player: every player rises on the floor's starts. Otherwise **GAME OVER** (\"THE GAUNT IS FED.\"), then each player whose score qualifies enters initials on the letter wheel with their own controller (E7), then the table, then the title.\n258\t- **High scores:** `E.Arcade` table `id: 'gauntletdown'`, mode `'descent'`, top 10: initials, score, class icon, deepest floor, continues used. Runs with any Dev cheat on are not recorded (a DEV badge says so).\n259\t- **Sessions:** no continue prompt: a fallen hero rises automatically after 5 s beside a living ally with 350 health and loses 250 points (not below 0). If every hero is down at once, the host finishes the round.\n260\t\n261\t### 4.11 Scoring\n262\t\n263\tKills (4.5), generators (25 × rank), treasure and food (4.7), exit bonus (4.9), treasure-room clear (+2000), the King (10,000), the Iron Gauntlet (+5000 to whoever grabs it). Scores are per player. The HUD shows each score; the floor card shows the round's per-player numbers.\n264\t\n265\t### 4.12 The narrator: \"The Gaunt\"\n266\t\n267\t- The dungeon itself speaks, in the source's style: short, booming, third person, darkly funny (lines in 5.6). Every line shows as a big caption (bottom centre, 2 lines at most, outlined, scale 2 on wide screens) and is spoken by the narrator voice: deep gibberish with an echo (4.21).\n268\t- **Queue rules:** three priorities (critical: dying, starving, shot food, the Tithe, deaths; event: pickups, firsts, traps, stairs; tip: teaching lines). At most one line every 1.2 s; a higher priority cuts a tip; each line has a cooldown (per hero for health lines: 20 s); teaching tips play once per game (kept in `E.store` so a second game skips them; Settings → Tips: On/Off).\n269\t- **Triggers:** health crossing 400, 200 and 100; the first of each item, monster and feature; shot food or flasks; the Tithe arriving, leaving and dying; the Bell; impatience stages; stairs; boss phases; game over; high score.\n270\t- In sessions the host decides lines about events (`say` events, 4.20) so every copy hears the same thing; a client's own teaching tips are local.\n271\t\n272\t### 4.13 Camera and local co-op\n273\t\n274\t- **One hero:** `game.follow(hero, { z: 12, lead: 12 })`.\n275\t- **Several local heroes share one screen**, as in the arcade: `game.cam.frame(livingHeroes, { margin: 64, zoom: [0.8, 1] })` and a **leash**: a hero can't move so that the party's bounding box would exceed the visible ground minus the margin. Measure the visible ground each frame from the four screen corners with `game.view.toGround(cam.x + sx, cam.y + sy)` (it depends on view, zoom, turn and screen shape), and cancel the part of a hero's step that would stretch the box past it. Fallen heroes don't hold the camera.\n276\t- **Scene camera:** `camera: { zoom: [0.75, 1.5], start: 1, tall: 1.25 }` (wheel, - and =, Settings).\n277\t- **Views:** Settings → Camera view (Three-quarter, Top-down, Isometric) calls `game.setView`; V cycles them in play.\n278\t- **Visibility:** heroes draw with `xray: { color: playerColour }`, so a hero behind a wall stays visible; each hero has a ground ring in its player colour and (Settings) a name tag.\n279\t- **Joining:** `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })` on class select and in play. A player who joins in play picks a free class on a small overlay over their new panel (the game keeps running), then drops in beside the party with full starting health. **Drop out:** the pause menu's \"Drop out (P2)\" (shown when a player other than 1 paused) removes that player (`game.removePlayer`). Joining is closed (`game.allowJoin(false)`) in the attract mode and in sessions.\n280\t- **Classes are unique** in local play (a taken card says TAKEN). With four players, all four classes play.\n281\t\n282\t### 4.14 HUD (canvas pixel art, anchored to `r.W`/`r.H`, clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n283\t\n284\t- **Player panels**, top edge, one per joined player (up to four, each about `r.W / 4` wide, 34 game pixels tall): a live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) on a disc in the player's colour, the class name, **health as a big number** (font scale 2; white, yellow under 400, flashing red under 200), the score, key and flask icons with counts, the amulet icon with its ring timer, special potion icons in a small row. Empty slots (local) pulse \"[Options]/[2] TO JOIN\"; fallen heroes show \"RISE: [Fire]\".\n285\t- **Centre top:** floor name; in sessions the round clock (from `AIHub.time()` and `limitMs`) and a compact scoreboard of every player (name, score) in seat colours.\n286\t- **Bottom centre:** narrator captions.\n287\t- **Around the hero:** the stair ring, the amulet ring, the \"ON THE MENU\" bell icon, a Queasy face.\n288\t- **Screen edges:** arrows to allies off screen (sessions) and to the stairs once found or after impatience.\n289\t- **Big centre text:** treasure-room clock, CONTINUE, countdowns.\n290\t- **10-foot rules:** nothing smaller than the 5×7 font at scale 1; at most three numbers per panel; no tables during play.\n291\t\n292\t### 4.15 Front-end screens (canvas pixel art; big; mouse, keys and controller)\n293\t\n294\t- **Boot:** the engine's boot screen with steps (\"Digging the Gaunt\", \"Setting the table\", \"Waking the ghosts\") and an error report if anything fails.\n295\t- **Title:** the GAUNTLETDOWN logo (`E.font.title`, a four-colour iron-and-gold gradient, extruded), a scene behind it: an iron gauntlet tumbling down an endless torch-lit shaft, the four heroes silhouetted at the edge. \"PRESS [✕]/[Enter]\" pulses. The engine version (`E.versionLabel()`) small at the bottom. Keep the top-right corner clear (the engine's menu and full-screen buttons).\n296\t- **Main menu:** START DESCENT, HOW TO PLAY, HIGH SCORES, SETTINGS (`game.menu('settings')`), ABOUT & CREDITS. (In Descent II after an ending: CONTINUE TO DESCENT II on top.)\n297\t- **Class select (\"CHOOSE YOUR FOOL\"):** four big cards, each with its live rig turning slowly (idle; it swings on focus), name and class, five stat rows as 1–5 pips (ARMOR, SHOTS, MELEE, MAGIC, SPEED) and a quip. Each joined player has a cursor in their colour; Fire locks a card; START begins once every joined player has locked. \"[Options]/[2] TO JOIN\" for empty seats. Hover focuses, click picks.\n298\t- **How to Play:** 8 paged cards (5.7), one idea per page, each with a live illustration (a rig, a sprite, a tiny scripted scene), left/right to page.\n299\t- **High Scores:** the `E.Arcade` table, drawn large.\n300\t- **About & Credits:** paged (5.8), including Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n301\t- Every screen: Back with ○/Esc/Backspace/right click; idle 10 s starts the attract mode.\n302\t\n303\t### 4.16 Pause menu and Settings\n304\t\n305\t- **Pause** (engine standard, on Esc/P/Options): Resume, How to Play, **Dev Tools**, Restart floor, Drop out (P2–P4), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title (the engine asks first). The pause menu's How to Play is the game's `E.Shell` help screen (`screens: { help: { keys, sections } }`): the eight cards of 5.7 as sections, with keys from `input.label()`, since the canvas scenes don't run while paused. `menu: { items: [...], controls: { fire: 'Fire', magic: 'Magic', plant: 'Plant' }, quit: 'title' }`. The engine says \"P2 PAUSED\" when player 2 paused.\n306\t- **Settings:** the engine's Display, Sound and Comfort groups (scaled for TV, E6), plus **Game**: Camera view; Button symbols (PlayStation default, Xbox; E5); Difficulty (Easy, Normal, Hard); Aim assist (Off, Low, High); Right stick fires (On); Ally stun (On); Narrator captions (On); Tips (On); Player names (On); HUD size (Normal, Large); Enhanced lighting (WebGPU where available; On on desktop). Sound gains **Voices** (E8). The engine's Controls screen handles rebinding, dead zone, vibration.\n307\t\n308\t### 4.17 Dev Tools (from the pause menu; not in sessions, not in attract)\n309\t\n310\tFour pages (E.Shell screens with the row widgets, E6), each one screen tall, navigable by controller, keys and mouse:\n311\t\n312\t1. **Cheats** (toggles; reset on every load): God mode (no damage, no drain); Noclip; Infinite keys and flasks; Freeze monsters; One-hit kills; Generators off; Show hitboxes; Show flow field; Show net stats (sessions are tested through the harness, but the overlay also works in a dev host); Show bot thoughts; Time scale (0.25, 0.5, 1, 2).\n313\t2. **Warp:** Floor 1–9, Treasure Room I and II, Boss phase 2, Boss phase 3, Ending, Game over, Descent II, Restart floor.\n314\t3. **Give and spawn:** +3 keys, +3 flasks, a roast, a stew, each amulet, every special, +1000 score, heal the party; spawn monster (type and rank selects, then \"Spawn 5 here\"), spawn a generator; kill all monsters; destroy all generators; open every door; reveal secrets; next impatience stage; start the attract mode now; Bot plays player 1 (toggle).\n315\t4. **Tuning:** a live slider for each † value in 4.24 (applied at once, saved), and **Reset tuning to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev tuning')`).\n316\t\n317\tWhile any cheat is on, the HUD shows a small DEV badge and high scores are not recorded.\n318\t\n319\t### 4.18 Attract mode and the autopilot\n320\t\n321\t- **Timer:** on any front-end screen, 10 s without input (no key, button, stick past the dead zone, click, wheel, or mouse movement over 4 px) starts the attract mode. **Any input** returns to the title at once and is consumed (it doesn't also pick a menu item).\n322\t- **The loop:** \"DEMO\" banner and a pulsing \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\". (1) **Floor 2**, 25 s: four bot heroes clear gnashers, melee, eat, open a door, use a flask. (2) **Floor 5**, 20 s: the Tithe, the Dinner Bell, force fields, stun runes. (3) **Floor 7**, 15 s: imps, fireballs, lava and ash. (4) **The banquet**, 20 s: King Famish in phase 2, heroes shooting the food. (5) High scores, 6 s. (6) The prologue, 8 s. (7) The title, 4 s. Then again from (1).\n323\t- **Cheats allowed** (TASK.md): bots are invulnerable, have infinite flasks, and are teleported to the next waypoint if stuck for 3 s. A director spawns monsters near the bots when the screen is quiet. Music and effects play at 60%.\n324\t- **The autopilot** (`31-bot.js`, adapted from Emberdeep's) produces intents from the sim's state. Goal priority each 0.25 s: (1) health under 250 and food within 20 tiles → go eat; (2) a monster within 7 tiles in sight → aim and fire (keep distance as Ranger or Hexer); (3) a generator within 10 tiles in sight → shoot it; (4) fewer keys than the doors on its route and a key reachable → fetch it; (5) a door it can open → open it; (6) treasure within 12 tiles → take it; (7) the stairs. Magic when 12 or more monsters are on screen. Each goal gets a single-source FlowField. Stuck (under 8 units of progress in 3 s): sidestep, then, if cheats are on, teleport to the next waypoint.\n325\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"d3c293ac-68f4-4ddb-b7b6-8184a2f2ecb5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:38.909Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-build--20261104-050250--x8ffc89-work/04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db/tool-results/bl5ye5sy8.txt","content":"## 1. The game on one page\n\n**Core loop (one sentence, as the engine's guide asks):** descend floor by floor through a starving dungeon, blasting hordes and the generators that breed them, grabbing keys, food and treasure before your ever-draining life force runs out: together, and racing each other for score.\n\n**Genre:** arcade co-op dungeon crawler: a top-down hack-and-shoot (\"hack-and-slash shooter\") with maze exploration. Catalogue genre: **Action**.\n**Perspective:** **three-quarter overhead** (the engine's `threequarter` view, 55° pitch): it shows wall faces and character faces (the N64-era *Gauntlet Legends* angle) while keeping the maze readable. **Top-down** (`topdown`, 80°) and **isometric** (`iso`) are selectable in Settings. The rules are the same in every view.\n**Players:** 1–4. Couch co-op with drop-in and drop-out (gamepads, and up to two players on one keyboard); online 1–4 through AI Hub sessions.\n**Session length:** a full descent is about 35–50 minutes (9 floors, 2 treasure rooms, a boss); an AI Hub round is 6 minutes.\n\n### What makes Gauntlet distinctive, and how this game captures it\n\n| Source trait | In Gauntletdown |\n|---|---|\n| Four archetype heroes with clearly different stats, up to four at once | Berserker, Shieldmaiden, Ranger, Hexer (original characters), each with its own armor, shot, melee, magic and speed; 1–4 players |\n| Health ticks down every second; food is life | **Life force** drains 1 per second; roasts, loaves and cider restore it; health is shown as a big number, like the arcade |\n| Endless hordes from generators | Six generator types breed monsters until destroyed; crowds jam corridors |\n| Monsters come in strength levels and weaken when hit | Ranks 3, 2, 1: a wounded rank-3 monster visibly shrinks to rank 2, then 1 |\n| Keys open doors; magic potions clear the screen | A key opens a whole run of doors; a **Blast Flask** strikes every monster on screen |\n| \"Don't shoot the food\"; shooting a potion wastes it | Cider and stew can be shot (and are destroyed); a shot flask detonates at half power |\n| Death: can't be shot, drains your health, only magic kills it | **The Tithe**, a reaper that drains up to 200 and only magic can kill |\n| The booming announcer (\"... needs food badly\", \"... shot the food\") | **The Gaunt**, the dungeon's own voice: terse booming callouts in the same style, with original lines, spoken in deep gibberish under big captions |\n| Exits, skip-exits, traps, transporters, treasure rooms, stun tiles, force fields | All present (4.8) |\n| Co-op that is also competitive | Individual scores; whoever takes the stairs gets the exit bonus; AI Hub standings are by score |\n| Insert-a-coin drop-in, a loop that never ends | Join any time; fallen heroes **rise again**; after the ending, **Descent II** loops the dungeon harder |\n| Walls turn into exits if you dawdle | The Gaunt grows impatient: doors open at 3:00, every wall becomes a stair at 4:00 |\n\n### Originality guardrails (non-negotiable)\n\nBuild an original game *in the genre* of Gauntlet, not a recreation of it (TASK.md and the system rules):\n- No names, characters, art, music, levels or exact lines from any Gauntlet game. Not Thor, Thyra, Merlin or Questor; not \"Warrior/Valkyrie/Wizard/Elf\" as the class set; not \"Wizard needs food, badly\", \"Elf shot the food\", \"Remember, don't shoot food\", or \"Shots do not hurt other players... yet\". The lines in 5.6 are original and follow the source's *style*: short, booming, third-person, darkly funny.\n- All floors are this plan's own layouts. All music is original composition. Monster designs are this plan's (hunger-themed: ghosts with gaping mouths, kitchen imps, frying-pan friars).\n- The title is a riff on the source's name, as TASK.md requires.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Deliverables and folder layout\n\n### The run folder (this folder)\n\n```\nPLAN.md, STAGE.md, TASK.md                              (given)\nGauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174804.html   <- the game, one file, works from file://\nexit-interview.json                                      <- written last (Appendix A), must parse as JSON\nGauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174804/      <- every dev file\n```\n\n### The dev subfolder\n\nStart it as a copy of the engine's `dist/handoff/` (sparse-clone it: `git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git` then `git sparse-checkout set dist/handoff`, and copy `dist/handoff/*` into the dev subfolder), so the engine's tools work with their own paths. Then add:\n\n```\n<dev>/\n  my-3d2dge.js          the full engine (every module included), PATCHED as listed in 3.5\n  ENGINE-CHANGES.md     each engine change: what, why, its test (feeds Engine Feedback)\n  API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, docs/, tools/, src/assets/ (from the handoff: references, tools, the asset store)\n  package.json          from the handoff (pins Playwright 1.63.0); `npm install` once\n  hub/                  session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md, fetched with\n                        curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/<file>\n  game/\n    src/NN-*.js         the game's source fragments (3.2), concatenated in name order into one IIFE\n    game.js             built from src/ (never edited by hand)\n    index.html          the dev page: session.js first in <head>, then my-3d2dge.js, then game.js\n  build.mjs             builds game/game.js and the single-file deliverable (3.6)\n  tests/                run.mjs (the one command) and the suites (section 8)\n  docs/DESIGNER.md      how to add a floor, a monster, an item or a line (the \"designer tools\" note)\n  shots/                screenshots for look review (not shipped)\n```\n\nThe handoff's template game goes: `game/game.js` is overwritten by `build.mjs`, and `game/test.mjs` (and `kits/`, once you have taken what you need) can be deleted. The deliverable is only the single HTML file; the dev folder is the workshop.\n\n### What the finished demo contains\n\nTitle screen with attract mode; main menu; class select; How to Play; High Scores; About/Credits (with the four feedback sections); 9 floors in three realms, 2 treasure rooms and a boss; an ending, credits and the Descent II loop; game over, continue and initials entry; the engine's pause menu, settings and controls (adjusted), plus **Dev Tools**; local co-op 1–4; AI Hub shared-world sessions 1–4; the touch-only notice. Audio entirely synthesized in code.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems and mechanics (the spec)\n\nAll distances are world units (one tile = 16). Speeds are units per second. Every number marked † is a `TUNE` entry (4.24) and a Dev slider.\n\n### 4.1 Floors, the map and the legend\n\n- A floor is a `def('floors', id, { name, realm, no, music, par, rank, genRank, specials: [], amulets: [], intro: [...], next, rows: [...] })`. `rows` are ASCII strings, all the same width, bordered by walls. The parser builds an `E.TileMap` (wall types per realm, `cut: true, cutH: 6` so walls in front of the camera drop low; `ao: 6`), the entity lists, door groups, trap groups, transporter pairs and beams.\n- **Wall height 24**, a little below a hero's head. Hero shots fly at z 12, so they pass over the banquet table (h 10) and are stopped by walls (the engine's `Bullets` already compare `map.heightAt` with the bullet's z).\n- Corridors are at least 2 tiles wide; rooms 6–14 tiles across. Floors range from 40×20 (the tutorial) to 64×44.\n\n**The legend (shared by every floor):**\n\n| Char | Meaning | Char | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `#` | wall (realm stone) | `@` | hero start (author 4; fewer are padded on free neighbours) |\n| `%` | accent wall (shelves, bone wall, iron) | `E` | stairs down (exit) |\n| `X` | cracked wall (4 HP, shots break it) | `2`–`9` | skip stairs to floor N |\n| `+` | door (iron bars); 4-connected runs open together | `O` | transporter pad (paired in reading order: 1st↔2nd, 3rd↔4th) |\n| `T` | trap wall, removed when any `^` plate is stepped on | `!` | stun rune |\n| `Y` | trap wall, removed when any `v` plate is stepped on | `s` | spikes (cycling) |\n| `?` | fake wall: drawn as a wall, walkable (a secret) | `\\|` `-` | force-field beam, vertical / horizontal (pylons drawn where it meets walls) |\n| `~` | lava or chasm (blocked floor, glows in the Furnace) | `^` `v` | pressure plates |\n| `.` | floor | `,` | floor variant (rug, dirt, bone dust) |\n| `k` | key | `f` | roast (+100, can't be shot) |\n| `b` | loaf (+50, can't be shot) | `j` | cider jug (+100, shootable) |\n| `z` | spoiled stew (poison, shootable) | `m` | Blast Flask (magic) |\n| `u` | special potion (type from `meta.specials`, reading order) | `a` | amulet (type from `meta.amulets`, reading order) |\n| `$` | gold | `*` | gem |\n| `h` | chest | `l` | locked chest (needs a key) |\n| `w` | crown | `B` | Dinner Bell |\n| `g` `n` `o` `i` `y` `x` `t` | monsters: hungerghost, gnasher, pot-lobber, cinder imp, fryar, snatcher, the Tithe (rank from `meta.rank`) | `G` `N` `L` `I` `F` `S` | generators: ash urn, gnasher den, crockery hutch, ember grate, candle shrine, sack heap (rank from `meta.genRank`) |\n| `K` | King Famish (boss floor) | `=` | banquet table (low wall, h 10) |\n| `P` | a table cell carrying a feast platter (+200, shootable) | `U` | a table cell carrying a soup tureen (the boss floor's ghost generator) |\n\nPer-cell overrides go in `meta.ranks: { 'x,y': 3 }`, set pieces in `meta.props: [[shapeId, cx, cy, facing]]`, snatcher escape points and boss spawn points in `meta.points`.\n\n- **Automatic decoration:** a deterministic pass (`E.hash2(cx, cy)`) puts a torch (`r.prop('torch', ..., { light: true })`) on about one wall face in six along open floor, and 3–8 realm props per room against walls (Larder: barrels, kegs, sacks, crates, hanging hams; Ossuary: skulls, bones, coffins, candelabras, cobwebs, urns; Furnace: braziers, fire drums, anvils, chains). Decoration goes only on empty floor cells beside walls (never on an item, monster, generator, plate, pad, rune, beam, spike or stairs cell). Props that block are made solid with `map.solid`, and the validator re-runs the solvability check (8.3) with them in place, so decoration can never cut a floor in two.\n\n### 4.2 Heroes\n\n| | **Berserker** | **Shieldmaiden** | **Ranger** | **Hexer** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Character | Brakka Ironbelly | Hilde Stoutheart | Fenn Quickfletch | Old Mother Wix |\n| Look | Humanoid `bulky` size 1.15, `weapon: 'axe'`, `hat: 'horned'`, fur cape, bare arms; red and brown | `heroic` 1.1, `weapon: 'sword'`, `offhand: 'shield'`, `hat: 'helmet'`, `hair: 'ponytail'`; blue and steel | `heroic` 1.05, `weapon: 'bow'`, hood, short cape, `sleeves: 'long'`; green and leather | `chibi` 1.05, `weapon: 'staff'`, `hat: 'pointed'`, `outfit: 'robe'`, `hunch: .3`, `face: { eyes: 'big' }`; yellow and purple |\n| Hub seat (colour) | 1 (red `#e8443a`) | 2 (blue `#3b82f6`) | 3 (green `#22c55e`) | 4 (yellow `#f5b700`) |\n| Move speed | 62 | 66 | 78 | 64 |\n| Armor (damage taken ×) | 0.75 | 0.60 | 0.90 | 1.00 |\n| Shot | spinning hand-axe | javelin | arrow | hex-bolt |\n| Shot damage | 3, pierces 1 foe | 2 | 1 | 2, plus 1 splash within 12 |\n| Shot speed / cooldown | 190 / 0.34 s | 240 / 0.27 s | 300 / 0.15 s | 220 / 0.26 s |\n| Melee damage per swing | 5 | 4 | 2 | 1.5 |\n| Melee moves (`E.MOVES`) | `overhead` → `spin` | `thrust` → `bash` (shield) | `jab` → `cross` (dagger) | `bash` (staff) |\n| Magic power (monsters / generators) | 1.0 / 1.0 | 1.4 / 1.0 | 1.7 / 1.0 | 2.5 / 2.0 |\n| Throw animation | `throw` | `throw` | bow draw (new spec, 4.23) | `cast` |\n| Voice | low, gruff | firm, mid | quick, light | high, cackling |\n\n- **Health (life force):** starts at 700†, no maximum (numbers above 9999 show as 9999+). Drains 1 per second† for every living hero, all the time on a floor (not on cards or menus).\n- **Shooting:** fire is held for auto-fire at the class's cooldown. The shot leaves the weapon hand (`rig.hand('R')`, or 8 ahead at z 12) in the aim direction; range 220 (its `life` is range ÷ speed). Shots are `E.Bullets` on the ground plane, `team: 'hero'`, `data: { owner, kind }`. They pass through allies (but see ally stun below).\n- **Smart melee:** when fire is pressed and a non-ghost monster is within reach (hero r + monster r + 8) inside ±50° of the aim, the hero swings its melee combo (`E.Combo`) instead of throwing. Melee hits everything in the arc (`attack.hits` with `E.inArc(hero, aim, m, 22, 1.2)`), with `game.hitFx`. Hungerghosts can't be struck: up close the hero throws point-blank instead.\n- **Plant:** holding Plant (Shift, L2) stops the hero, which turns with the movement input and keeps firing: the arcade \"stand and shoot\" stance. **Keyboard-only firing** (fire from a key while mouse aim is off, below) plants automatically, as in the arcade.\n- **Aim:** right stick: its direction through `game.view.screenDirToGround` (pushing it past 0.5 also fires, a setting); mouse: toward the ground point under the cursor (`game.mouseGround()`), with a reticle, while `input.aimSource === 'mouse'` and the mouse moved in the last 3 s or a mouse button is firing (the engine's `aimSource` only changes on mouse or pad input, never on keys, so a stale cursor must not keep aiming); otherwise the hero's facing (the last movement direction). **Aim assist** (Off / Low 8° / High 16°): snaps to the nearest visible monster or generator within that cone and 200 units.\n- **Magic (Blast Flask):** pressing Magic with at least one flask uses it: every monster inside the user's screen rectangle (the shared screen in local co-op; the user's own view in a session) takes `4 × magic power` damage (rounded up); generators there take `2 × magic-vs-generators`; the Tithe dies. A white flash, a shockwave ring, a choir sting, the hero's `cast` pose.\n- **Carry limits:** 9 keys and 9 flasks (12 with Deep Pockets). Pickups over the limit stay on the floor.\n- **Ally stun:** from floor 6 on (and in Descent II), a hero shot that touches an ally stuns that ally for 0.35 s (Settings: Ally stun On/Off; default On). The narrator announces it at floor 6's start.\n- **Starving look:** below 200 health the rig hunches (`hunch` rises with hunger), the walk slows its bob, and a heartbeat plays for local players.\n\n### 4.3 Controls and prompts (10-foot, controller-first)\n\nThe game is designed around a PS5 DualSense in the browser's standard mapping, played on a TV; keyboard and mouse get the keys PC players expect for a twin-stick shooter, on the same screens. Custom input preset `GD_INPUT` (the engine's menu actions are added by the engine):\n\n| Action | Keyboard and mouse (player 1) | DualSense | Xbox labels (setting) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Move | W A S D (and arrows when alone on the keyboard) | Left stick, D-pad | Left stick, D-pad |\n| Aim | Mouse | Right stick | Right stick |\n| Fire (hold) | Left click, Space, J | R2, ✕ | RT, A |\n| Magic | Right click, Q, K | △, R1 | Y, RB |\n| Plant (hold) | Shift | L2 | LT |\n| Change camera view | V | (Settings) | (Settings) |\n| Zoom | Wheel, - and = | (Settings) | (Settings) |\n| Pause and menu | Esc, P | Options | Menu |\n| Menus | arrows / mouse hover and click, Enter, Esc or Backspace | D-pad/stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | A confirm, B back |\n| Join (local) | 2 (the keyboard's right half) | Options on a free controller | Menu on a free controller |\n\n- In `GD_INPUT`, list each action's gamepad codes with the prompt you want first (Fire: `Pad7` before `Pad0`, so prompts say R2; Magic: `Pad3` before `Pad5`, so they say △), since a prompt shows an action's first code for the device.\n- A second keyboard player (who joined with 2) gets the right half, as the engine splits it: arrows to move, then `.` `/` `,` for Fire, Magic, Plant (and the numpad). Player 1 keeps W A S D with F G H for the same three, plus the mouse.\n- **Create (Share) does nothing**: in sessions the hub owns Create + Options (engine change E4).\n- **Prompts follow the device used last** (`input.label(action)`): PlayStation glyphs for any controller by default (✕ ○ □ △, L1/R1/L2/R2, Options), Xbox glyphs (A B X Y, LB/RB/LT/RT, Menu) with Settings → Button symbols, key names and \"Left click\"/\"Right click\" for keyboard and mouse. Never hard-code a key in text: every prompt, card and help page is built from `label()`. Each local player's panel shows that player's own prompts.\n- **The mouse in menus:** hover moves the focus, a click picks (E.Menu does this; class cards and How to Play pages must too). **The mouse in the world:** the reticle; hovering a monster or generator outlines it and shows its name and rank; clicking fires at it.\n- **Touch:** no touch controls anywhere (4.19).\n\n### 4.4 Combat and damage\n\n- **Monster HP** is `baseHP × rank`; its **rank** is `ceil(hp / baseHP)` after each hit. When the rank drops, the rig shrinks (scale 1.15 → 1.0 → 0.88) and its palette pales, with a puff: the arcade's \"level\" system made visible.\n- **Hero damage taken** = monster damage × class armor × difficulty × Iron Brew. Hero hit: `hurt` flinch, a red flash on the panel, a small knockback, a pain bark (Babble), a 0.25 s grace before the same monster's contact damage can hit again.\n- **Heroes and monsters block each other.** A hero can be boxed in by a horde, as in the arcade; fight out or use magic. Resolve circle overlaps every step with an `E.SpatialHash` (cell 32): monsters push each other apart softly; heroes are pushed out of monsters.\n- **Kills:** score = monster points × the rank it spawned at; `game.hitFx` on every hit; a death effect per type (ghost: a wail and a puff; gnasher: a tumble, `pose: 'down'`, then a fade; imp: a small explosion; fryar: smoke; Tithe: a bone burst).\n- **Hit feedback:** hit-stop 0.03–0.05 s on melee, shake on magic and generator deaths, damage numbers only on generators and the boss (hordes would drown the screen in numbers).\n\n### 4.5 Monsters\n\n| Monster | Char | Generator | HP / rank | Speed r1/r2/r3 | Attack | Damage r1/r2/r3 | Points / rank | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Hungerghost** | `g` | Ash Urn `G` | 2 | 40 / 46 / 52 | flies into a hero, then vanishes | 10 / 20 / 30 | 10 | Can't be struck in melee; floats over runes and spikes; paths around walls like everyone |\n| **Gnasher** | `n` | Gnasher Den `N` | 2 | 34 / 38 / 42 | club swing: 0.32 s wind-up, reach 14, every 0.9 s | 6 / 8 / 10 | 10 | The horde; club raised high in the wind-up |\n| **Pot-Lobber** | `o` | Crockery Hutch `L` | 2 | 30 / 34 / 38 (flees at 46) | lobs a crock over walls (`E.arc`, apex 40, range 130) every 2.2 / 1.9 / 1.6 s at the hero's position plus lead; a shadow marks the landing 0.6 s ahead | 8 / 10 / 12 splash within 12 | 15 | Keeps 70–110 away, flees inside 56; its crocks are `Bullets` with `grav` and break on landing |\n| **Cinder Imp** | `i` | Ember Grate `I` | 3 | 36 / 40 / 44 | bite (reach 10); fireball (speed 110, only with sight, every 1.8 s, 0.35 s mouth glow first) | bite 6 / 8 / 10, fireball 8 / 10 / 12 | 20 | Fireballs destroy shootable food they hit |\n| **Fryar** | `y` | Candle Shrine `F` | 3 | 36 / 40 / 44 | frying-pan smack, 0.3 s wind-up | 8 / 10 / 12 | 25 | Visible 2.0 s, invisible 1.4 s (can't be hit; shots pass through); reappears up to 48 closer along its path, with smoke |\n| **Snatcher** | `x` | Sack Heap `S` | 3 (rank 1 only) | 72 | steals on touch: a flask, else a key, else the active amulet | none | 100, plus the item back | Then flees to its heap or the nearest `meta.points.escape`; escapes with the item unless killed (then drops it) |\n| **The Tithe** | `t` | none (placed, or the impatience timer) | immune | 52 | drains while touching: 6 health per 0.1 s, at most 200 per hero | drain | 1000 × (1–5), drawn from `rng.sim` | Only magic kills it (a flask, or a shot flask's blast); shots clink off; vanishes when it has taken 200 from a hero (\"THE TITHE IS PAID\") |\n| **Dinner Bell** | `B` | none | object | none | a hero who touches it rings it and is **ON THE MENU** | none | none | Every monster targets that hero for 12 s, or until they touch an ally, who is then on the menu (a co-op hot potato); one ring per floor |\n| **King Famish** | `K` | boss | 400 × (1 + 0.5 × (players − 1)) | 30 | plates, stomp, eating, charge, fog (5.3) | 10–15 per attack; fog triples the drain | 10,000 | Three phases (5.3) |\n\n**AI (23-sim-monsters.js):**\n- **Navigation:** one multi-source `FlowField` toward every living hero (E1), rebuilt when a hero changes cell; each monster steps along `flow.dir`. While the Bell marks a hero, a single-source field toward that hero is used instead. Snatchers fleeing and lobbers keeping their distance use their own fields (toward the escape point; away from the hero by climbing the distance gradient).\n- **Activation:** monsters farther than 20 tiles from every hero stand still (they wait in the dark, as in the arcade).\n- **Telegraphs:** every enemy attack winds up visibly (raised club, mouth glow, landing shadow, pan drawn back) for at least 0.3 s, longer than any hero swing, as the engine's animation guide asks.\n- **Amulet reactions:** Veil: monsters lose track of that hero unless adjacent and wander. Stench: monsters flee from that hero within 64.\n- **Hazards:** force fields hurt monsters too (lure hordes through them); spikes and lava don't affect ghosts.\n\n### 4.6 Generators\n\n- HP `4 × rank`† (Dev multiplier); they take shot, melee and magic damage, and lose a rank, with a damage state, every 4 HP. Spawn interval r1 3.0 s, r2 2.2 s, r3 1.5 s (× spawn interval multiplier†, ÷ (1 + 0.25 × (players − 1))). A generator spawns only when a hero is within 15 tiles, it has fewer than 8 living children, and the floor is under its monster cap† (140; 100 in sessions). New monsters emerge into a free neighbouring cell over 0.4 s (rising from the generator with dust) at the generator's current rank.\n- Destroyed: debris, a crumble sound, 25 × rank points, and a 10% chance to drop a loaf.\n- Generators are static circular obstacles (r 7) in the same overlap pass as bodies, not TileMap walls, so destroying one needs no map change; shots hit them through `shots.hit`.\n- Art (4.22): Ash Urn (ghosts), Gnasher Den (gnashers), Crockery Hutch (lobbers), Ember Grate (imps, flat and glowing, shoot it from any side), Candle Shrine (fryars), Sack Heap (snatchers), Soup Tureen (the boss's ghosts). Each has three damage states (intact, cracked, crumbling) as shape params, and breathes (a slow scale pulse) while it spawns.\n\n### 4.7 Items\n\n| Item | Char | Effect | Shootable | Points |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Key | `k` | +1 key (limit 9) | no | 0 |\n| Roast | `f` | +100 health† | no | 10 |\n| Loaf | `b` | +50 health | no | 5 |\n| Cider jug | `j` | +100 health | yes: destroyed, and the narrator names the culprit | 10 |\n| Spoiled stew | `z` | −50 health and Queasy (move × 0.6 for 4 s, green face) | yes: destroying it is good | 0 |\n| Blast Flask | `m` | +1 flask (limit 9) | yes: detonates at half the shooter's magic power within 80 | 0 |\n| Special potion | `u` | permanent upgrade for the rest of the game (below) | no | 250 |\n| Amulet | `a` | a 20 s power (below) | no | 100 |\n| Gold | `$` | | no | 100 |\n| Gem | `*` | | no | 250 |\n| Chest | `h` | opens on touch (lid tween, coins burst) | no | 500 |\n| Locked chest | `l` | needs and uses a key; drops a flask, a roast or a key | no | 1000 |\n| Crown | `w` | | no | 2500 |\n| Feast platter | `P` | +200 health (reachable from beside the table); King Famish eats them | yes | 20 |\n\nPickups happen on touch (hero r + 4). Food shows a crunchy \"chomp\" (squash and stretch, crumbs, a rising +100).\n\n**Special potions** (once per hero per type; icons under the panel): **Iron Brew** (damage taken × 0.8), **Ogre Ale** (melee × 1.5), **Quickshot Tonic** (cooldown × 0.75, shot speed × 1.2), **Hardshot Draught** (shot damage +1), **Witchwater** (magic × 1.5), **Featherfoot Cordial** (speed × 1.12), **Deep Pockets** (limits +3).\n\n**Amulets** (20 s each, a ring timer on the panel and around the hero): **Veil** (monsters lose track of you; drawn half-transparent), **Ironskin** (no damage; drain continues; gold shimmer), **Stench** (monsters flee from you; green fumes), **Ricochet** (shots bounce off walls up to 3 times, E3), **Rending** (shots pierce every monster and deal +1).\n\n### 4.8 Level features\n\n| Feature | Behaviour |\n|---|---|\n| Doors `+` | A hero with a key who pushes into a door cell (within r + 3) opens the whole 4-connected run and uses one key. The bars rise over 0.4 s (`map.set(cx, cy, 0)` per cell, plus a bars sprite that slides up) |\n| Cracked walls `X` | 4 HP; any hero shot (via `onWall`, E3) or melee damages them; they collapse into rubble floor with dust. Hide shortcuts and stashes |\n| Fake walls `?` | Drawn exactly as walls; walkable; shimmer when touched; the first one found triggers \"THAT WALL WAS LYING.\" |\n| Trap plates `^` `v` | One-shot: stepping on any `^` removes every `T` wall (crumble, a rumble); `v` does the same for `Y`. Traps release hordes or reveal treasure |\n| Transporters `O` | Stepping on a pad moves the hero to its pair with a swirl (0.6 s cooldown, 0.5 s invulnerable on arrival). Monsters don't use them |\n| Stun runes `!` | Heroes stepping on one are stunned 0.8 s (can't move or fire), then immune to runes for 1.5 s |\n| Force fields `\\|` `-` | Beams cycle 2 s on, 2 s off, flickering for 0.4 s before switching on. On: 12 damage and knockback to anything that touches (monsters too) |\n| Spikes `s` | Cycle 1.6 s (0.5 s up, with a 0.25 s tremble before); 15 damage |\n| Lava `~` | Blocked floor; glows (floor texels with glow, lights); heat shimmer under GPU lighting |\n| Stairs `E` | Stand on the stairs for 1.0 s† (a ring fills around the hero; stepping off cancels) and **everyone** descends; the stair-taker gets the exit bonus |\n| Skip stairs `2`–`9` | The same, to floor N (\"TOOK THE SHORT WAY DOWN\"); a carved number shows the target. Floors and treasure rooms in between are skipped; a realm card still plays when the skip enters a new realm |\n| Impatience | At 150 s† \"THE GAUNT GROWS IMPATIENT\"; at 180 s† every door opens; at 240 s every wall becomes a stair (wall faces glow; pushing into any wall for 1 s descends). From floor 5, the Tithe arrives at 120 s† if none is on the floor |\n| Treasure rooms | A 30 s† clock (big, top centre); treasure everywhere, no monsters, drain continues; the stairs are open. When the clock ends, \"THE HOARD SLAMS SHUT\" and everyone moves on. Taking every treasure: +2000 to whoever took the last |\n\n### 4.9 Floor flow\n\n1. **Floor card** (on entering): realm art behind, \"FLOOR 2\" big, the floor's name, the narrator's intro line (spoken), and for floors after the first, three numbers per player (score, kills, treasure). Continues on Fire/✕/Enter or after 5 s. In sessions the card is a 2 s banner and play never waits.\n2. **Play** until the stairs. Heroes start on the `@` cells.\n3. **Descent:** an iris transition (`game.go(..., { fade: 'iris', at: stairTaker })`), the heroes sink into the stairs, a descending arpeggio.\n4. **Exit bonus** to the stair-taker: 500 + 5 per second under the floor's `par` (default 150 s).\n5. **Realm cards** before floor 1, after each treasure room (entering realms II and III) and before floor 9: a short vignette (the party slides down a chute) and the realm's line (5.1).\n\n### 4.10 Death, rising again, continue, game over, high scores\n\n- **A hero falls** at 0 health: `pose: 'die'` (stagger, knees, topple), a ghostly wisp rises, \"BERSERKER HAS BEEN EATEN.\" Its panel shows **RISE: [Fire]**. Any time later, Fire brings it back beside a living ally with the starting health; the player's continues count goes up and their score is kept (the arcade's drop-in, without coins).\n- **Everyone down:** \"CONTINUE? 10\" (`E.Arcade` continue countdown). Fire or Start from any player: every player rises on the floor's starts. Otherwise **GAME OVER** (\"THE GAUNT IS FED.\"), then each player whose score qualifies enters initials on the letter wheel with their own controller (E7), then the table, then the title.\n- **High scores:** `E.Arcade` table `id: 'gauntletdown'`, mode `'descent'`, top 10: initials, score, class icon, deepest floor, continues used. Runs with any Dev cheat on are not recorded (a DEV badge says so).\n- **Sessions:** no continue prompt: a fallen hero rises automatically after 5 s beside a living ally with 350 health and loses 250 points (not below 0). If every hero is down at once, the host finishes the round.\n\n### 4.11 Scoring\n\nKills (4.5), generators (25 × rank), treasure and food (4.7), exit bonus (4.9), treasure-room clear (+2000), the King (10,000), the Iron Gauntlet (+5000 to whoever grabs it). Scores are per player. The HUD shows each score; the floor card shows the round's per-player numbers.\n\n### 4.12 The narrator: \"The Gaunt\"\n\n- The dungeon itself speaks, in the source's style: short, booming, third person, darkly funny (lines in 5.6). Every line shows as a big caption (bottom centre, 2 lines at most, outlined, scale 2 on wide screens) and is spoken by the narrator voice: deep gibberish with an echo (4.21).\n- **Queue rules:** three priorities (critical: dying, starving, shot food, the Tithe, deaths; event: pickups, firsts, traps, stairs; tip: teaching lines). At most one line every 1.2 s; a higher priority cuts a tip; each line has a cooldown (per hero for health lines: 20 s); teaching tips play once per game (kept in `E.store` so a second game skips them; Settings → Tips: On/Off).\n- **Triggers:** health crossing 400, 200 and 100; the first of each item, monster and feature; shot food or flasks; the Tithe arriving, leaving and dying; the Bell; impatience stages; stairs; boss phases; game over; high score.\n- In sessions the host decides lines about events (`say` events, 4.20) so every copy hears the same thing; a client's own teaching tips are local.\n\n### 4.13 Camera and local co-op\n\n- **One hero:** `game.follow(hero, { z: 12, lead: 12 })`.\n- **Several local heroes share one screen**, as in the arcade: `game.cam.frame(livingHeroes, { margin: 64, zoom: [0.8, 1] })` and a **leash**: a hero can't move so that the party's bounding box would exceed the visible ground minus the margin. Measure the visible ground each frame from the four screen corners with `game.view.toGround(cam.x + sx, cam.y + sy)` (it depends on view, zoom, turn and screen shape), and cancel the part of a hero's step that would stretch the box past it. Fallen heroes don't hold the camera.\n- **Scene camera:** `camera: { zoom: [0.75, 1.5], start: 1, tall: 1.25 }` (wheel, - and =, Settings).\n- **Views:** Settings → Camera view (Three-quarter, Top-down, Isometric) calls `game.setView`; V cycles them in play.\n- **Visibility:** heroes draw with `xray: { color: playerColour }`, so a hero behind a wall stays visible; each hero has a ground ring in its player colour and (Settings) a name tag.\n- **Joining:** `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })` on class select and in play. A player who joins in play picks a free class on a small overlay over their new panel (the game keeps running), then drops in beside the party with full starting health. **Drop out:** the pause menu's \"Drop out (P2)\" (shown when a player other than 1 paused) removes that player (`game.removePlayer`). Joining is closed (`game.allowJoin(false)`) in the attract mode and in sessions.\n- **Classes are unique** in local play (a taken card says TAKEN). With four players, all four classes play.\n\n### 4.14 HUD (canvas pixel art, anchored to `r.W`/`r.H`, clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n\n- **Player panels**, top edge, one per joined player (up to four, each about `r.W / 4` wide, 34 game pixels tall): a live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) on a disc in the player's colour, the class name, **health as a big number** (font scale 2; white, yellow under 400, flashing red under 200), the score, key and flask icons with counts, the amulet icon with its ring timer, special potion icons in a small row. Empty slots (local) pulse \"[Options]/[2] TO JOIN\"; fallen heroes show \"RISE: [Fire]\".\n- **Centre top:** floor name; in sessions the round clock (from `AIHub.time()` and `limitMs`) and a compact scoreboard of every player (name, score) in seat colours.\n- **Bottom centre:** narrator captions.\n- **Around the hero:** the stair ring, the amulet ring, the \"ON THE MENU\" bell icon, a Queasy face.\n- **Screen edges:** arrows to allies off screen (sessions) and to the stairs once found or after impatience.\n- **Big centre text:** treasure-room clock, CONTINUE, countdowns.\n- **10-foot rules:** nothing smaller than the 5×7 font at scale 1; at most three numbers per panel; no tables during play.\n\n### 4.15 Front-end screens (canvas pixel art; big; mouse, keys and controller)\n\n- **Boot:** the engine's boot screen with steps (\"Digging the Gaunt\", \"Setting the table\", \"Waking the ghosts\") and an error report if anything fails.\n- **Title:** the GAUNTLETDOWN logo (`E.font.title`, a four-colour iron-and-gold gradient, extruded), a scene behind it: an iron gauntlet tumbling down an endless torch-lit shaft, the four heroes silhouetted at the edge. \"PRESS [✕]/[Enter]\" pulses. The engine version (`E.versionLabel()`) small at the bottom. Keep the top-right corner clear (the engine's menu and full-screen buttons).\n- **Main menu:** START DESCENT, HOW TO PLAY, HIGH SCORES, SETTINGS (`game.menu('settings')`), ABOUT & CREDITS. (In Descent II after an ending: CONTINUE TO DESCENT II on top.)\n- **Class select (\"CHOOSE YOUR FOOL\"):** four big cards, each with its live rig turning slowly (idle; it swings on focus), name and class, five stat rows as 1–5 pips (ARMOR, SHOTS, MELEE, MAGIC, SPEED) and a quip. Each joined player has a cursor in their colour; Fire locks a card; START begins once every joined player has locked. \"[Options]/[2] TO JOIN\" for empty seats. Hover focuses, click picks.\n- **How to Play:** 8 paged cards (5.7), one idea per page, each with a live illustration (a rig, a sprite, a tiny scripted scene), left/right to page.\n- **High Scores:** the `E.Arcade` table, drawn large.\n- **About & Credits:** paged (5.8), including Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n- Every screen: Back with ○/Esc/Backspace/right click; idle 10 s starts the attract mode.\n\n### 4.16 Pause menu and Settings\n\n- **Pause** (engine standard, on Esc/P/Options): Resume, How to Play, **Dev Tools**, Restart floor, Drop out (P2–P4), Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title (the engine asks first). The pause menu's How to Play is the game's `E.Shell` help screen (`screens: { help: { keys, sections } }`): the eight cards of 5.7 as sections, with keys from `input.label()`, since the canvas scenes don't run while paused. `menu: { items: [...], controls: { fire: 'Fire', magic: 'Magic', plant: 'Plant' }, quit: 'title' }`. The engine says \"P2 PAUSED\" when player 2 paused.\n- **Settings:** the engine's Display, Sound and Comfort groups (scaled for TV, E6), plus **Game**: Camera view; Button symbols (PlayStation default, Xbox; E5); Difficulty (Easy, Normal, Hard); Aim assist (Off, Low, High); Right stick fires (On); Ally stun (On); Narrator captions (On); Tips (On); Player names (On); HUD size (Normal, Large); Enhanced lighting (WebGPU where available; On on desktop). Sound gains **Voices** (E8). The engine's Controls screen handles rebinding, dead zone, vibration.\n\n### 4.17 Dev Tools (from the pause menu; not in sessions, not in attract)\n\nFour pages (E.Shell screens with the row widgets, E6), each one screen tall, navigable by controller, keys and mouse:\n\n1. **Cheats** (toggles; reset on every load): God mode (no damage, no drain); Noclip; Infinite keys and flasks; Freeze monsters; One-hit kills; Generators off; Show hitboxes; Show flow field; Show net stats (sessions are tested through the harness, but the overlay also works in a dev host); Show bot thoughts; Time scale (0.25, 0.5, 1, 2).\n2. **Warp:** Floor 1–9, Treasure Room I and II, Boss phase 2, Boss phase 3, Ending, Game over, Descent II, Restart floor.\n3. **Give and spawn:** +3 keys, +3 flasks, a roast, a stew, each amulet, every special, +1000 score, heal the party; spawn monster (type and rank selects, then \"Spawn 5 here\"), spawn a generator; kill all monsters; destroy all generators; open every door; reveal secrets; next impatience stage; start the attract mode now; Bot plays player 1 (toggle).\n4. **Tuning:** a live slider for each † value in 4.24 (applied at once, saved), and **Reset tuning to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev tuning')`).\n\nWhile any cheat is on, the HUD shows a small DEV badge and high scores are not recorded.\n\n### 4.18 Attract mode and the autopilot\n\n- **Timer:** on any front-end screen, 10 s without input (no key, button, stick past the dead zone, click, wheel, or mouse movement over 4 px) starts the attract mode. **Any input** returns to the title at once and is consumed (it doesn't also pick a menu item).\n- **The loop:** \"DEMO\" banner and a pulsing \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\". (1) **Floor 2**, 25 s: four bot heroes clear gnashers, melee, eat, open a door, use a flask. (2) **Floor 5**, 20 s: the Tithe, the Dinner Bell, force fields, stun runes. (3) **Floor 7**, 15 s: imps, fireballs, lava and ash. (4) **The banquet**, 20 s: King Famish in phase 2, heroes shooting the food. (5) High scores, 6 s. (6) The prologue, 8 s. (7) The title, 4 s. Then again from (1).\n- **Cheats allowed** (TASK.md): bots are invulnerable, have infinite flasks, and are teleported to the next waypoint if stuck for 3 s. A director spawns monsters near the bots when the screen is quiet. Music and effects play at 60%.\n- **The autopilot** (`31-bot.js`, adapted from Emberdeep's) produces intents from the sim's state. Goal priority each 0.25 s: (1) health under 250 and food within 20 tiles → go eat; (2) a monster within 7 tiles in sight → aim and fire (keep distance as Ranger or Hexer); (3) a generator within 10 tiles in sight → shoot it; (4) fewer keys than the doors on its route and a key reachable → fetch it; (5) a door it can open → open it; (6) treasure within 12 tiles → take it; (7) the stairs. Magic when 12 or more monsters are on screen. Each goal gets a single-source FlowField. Stuck (under 8 units of progress in 3 s): sidestep, then, if cheats are on, teleport to the next waypoint.\n","numLines":325,"startLine":1,"totalLines":325}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FTuG9ozKeXfoxaXViKG9kH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
