{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrejDEhggZtHUkojCFR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LAJSni58h4hox92AfUv3RZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/s55/engine/dist/handoff; sed -n 1135,1162p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-500; grep -n \"pointer()\\|clicked()\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300 | head -5; grep -n \"game.menu(\\|menu: {\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300 | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2141,"cache_read_input_tokens":109926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2141},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"66c26a95-5594-425a-a8a2-c8578b296157","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:58.580Z","request_id":"req_011CghreiwN4wu5FfvncB8Uy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LAJSni58h4hox92AfUv3RZ":{"command":"cd /tmp/s55/engine/dist/handoff; sed -n 1135,1162p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-500; grep -n \"pointer()\\|clicked()\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300 | head -5; grep -n \"game.menu(\\|menu: {\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300 | head"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LAJSni58h4hox92AfUv3RZ","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n- `menu.game`: its game\n- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n- `E.ui`: pixel-drawn interface pieces for r.overlay\n- `E.ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, frac, color = '#e0463c', o = {})`: a bar (a meter: health, magic, stamina, a boss's): ui.bar(g, x, y, w, h, 0..1, '#e0463c')\n- `E.ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, o = {})`: window frame: ui.box(g, x, y, w, h, { bg, border, shadow, gradient }) bg: one color (drawn as a soft top-to-bottom gradient, like Final Fantasy windows) or [top, bottom] colors. gradient: false for a flat fill.\n- `E.ui.counter(g, x, y, label, value, color = '#ffffff', o = {})`: label + value, e.g. ui.counter(g, 4, 4, 'RUPEES', 12)\n- `E.ui.hearts(g, x, y, hp, max, o = {})`: row of hearts: hp and max in hearts (halves allowed, e.g. 2.5 of 3)\n\n## 21d. Shell\n\n282:- `input.clicked()` †: where a click or tap on the canvas landed, in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space: r.W, r.H), during the step after it lifted (a press that drags away, like the touch stick's, is none); else null. Menus and dialogs answer to it; a HUD button of your own can: if (hit(inpu\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game who\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (men\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050250__x8ffc89/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"52614260-83ce-44aa-b3d7-b0eafbfc8087","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:04:58.601Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n- `menu.game`: its game\n- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixel