{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JHhsxbpSNjXDqBwSNHUuTA","type":"tool_result","content":"514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1082:- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n7640:   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n7643:    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \"' + song + '\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\n7701:    if (typeof song === 'string') song = E.songs[song];\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050250__x8ffc89/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"e1ddd5ac-173e-497e-bdf0-ff26c02a4000","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:07:47.798Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens: C4 F#3 Bb2 = note, '-' holds the previous note, '.' = rest, '|' is ignored (bar lines). steps = steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Each track loops on its own length within the song's (len: steps, else its longest track's); a track may have a name, and on: false starts it silent (a layer that audio.layer brings in). THE MUSIC CLOCK: a song starts at the game's time and where it is is game time (audio.pos, headless too: the same steps hear the same beats); the sound follows that clock. o: { loop, sync: true (it pauses with the game, on game.time; else it plays on through a pause, on game.real), fade: seconds (a crossfade from the song playing), restart: true (again from its start, though it is the one playing) }. E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music: a rhythm game's calls and claps) }\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1082:- `E.Backdrop.presets` †: the preset names, all ten: day, dusk, night, castle-night, city-night, desert, forest, ocean, cave, space\n7640:   * E.songs has ready-made loops: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory.\n7643:    if (typeof song === 'string') { const s = E.songs[song]; if (!s) { warn('song:' + song, 'unknown song \"' + song + '\". Built in: ' + Object.keys(E.songs).join(', ')); return; } song = s; }\n7701:    if (typeof song === 'string') song = E.songs[song];","stderr":"\nShell cwd was re