{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghukqSorL6CxPVVZyQTo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TmzqSvesejoyb8KCMw8Trc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050250__x8ffc89/work && sed -n 1,200p TASK.md | head -c 4200 | tail -c 2300; echo; sed -n 925,953p PLAN.md | cut -c1-400"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2808,"cache_read_input_tokens":383790,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2808},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"b655e05f-bab9-49ab-8ee9-2330f9419214","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:45:30.960Z","request_id":"req_011Cghukq4ypDgwZgyB4sjCT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TmzqSvesejoyb8KCMw8Trc":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050250__x8ffc89/work && sed -n 1,200p TASK.md | head -c 4200 | tail -c 2300; echo; sed -n 925,953p PLAN.md | cut -c1-400"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TmzqSvesejoyb8KCMw8Trc","type":"tool_result","content":"processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state (the engine’s game.advance and game.debug, as in game/test.mjs), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game. \n\nM\n## 9. Done checklist (every TASK.md requirement, and where it is met)\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Met by |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective that fit the source | Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead (1, 4.13) |\n| Title: a riff, 50 brainstormed, picked with a real RNG | Gauntletdown (top of this plan) |\n| Single HTML named per TASK.md in the root; dev files in the subfolder | 2, 3.6 |\n| Built on my-3D2dge `dist/handoff`, engine changes allowed | 3.1, 3.5 |\n| Engine's native style plus new art for the source's feel | 4.22 |\n| Performance budget unlimited: as much detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows as needed; no FPS work | 4.22, 7 (Crowds) |\n| Engine's native animation plus new animations | 4.23 |\n| All music, sound and voices in code; gibberish voices | 4.21 |\n| AI Hub integration, and the game on its own | 4.20, 8.6 |\n| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics; polished vertical slice; infrastructure for more | 4, 5, registries (3.2), `docs/DESIGNER.md` |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset to defaults | 4.17 |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menus; any input exits; may cheat | 4.18, 8.4, 8.7 |\n| Narrative tone like the source's | 4.12, 5.1, 5.6 |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs, Xbox option | 4.3, 4.14, 4.15, E5, E6 |\n| No dense web-style data screens | 4.14, 4.15, 5.8 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, the notice, the settings button, attract runs | 4.19, 8.7 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | 6 (cut list removes whole features only) |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and an About/Credits screen | 5.8, Appendix B |\n| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parsing as JSON | Appendix A (check with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`) |\n| Headless testing, a scripted playthrough, one command printing only failures and a count | 8 |\n| Server on 127.0.0.1, port 0, confirm the page, stop only your own PIDs | 8.6 |\n| No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit | 0 |\n\n---","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04adf679-869d-4bcd-bcf3-495063b939db","uuid":"54065198-e320-4160-89f8-2fe8b02866e8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:45:30.983Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state (the engine’s game.advance and game.debug, as in game/test.mjs), including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game. \n\nM\n## 9. Done checklist (every TASK.md requirement, and where it is met)\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Met by |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective that fit the source | Arcade co-op dungeon crawler, three-quarter overhead (1, 4.13) |\n| Title: a riff, 50 brainstormed, picked with a real RNG | Gauntletdown (top of this plan) |\n| Single HTML named per TASK.md in the root; dev files in the subfolder | 2, 3.6 |\n| Built on my-3D2dge `dist/handoff`, engine changes allowed | 3.1, 3.5 |\n| Engine's native style plus new art for the source's feel | 4.22 |\n| Performance budget unlimited: as much detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows as needed; no FPS work | 4.22, 7 (Crowds) |\n| Engine's native animation plus new animations | 4.23 |\n| All music, sound and voices in code; gibberish voices | 4.21 |\n| AI Hub integration, and the game on its own | 4.20, 8.6 |\n| Feature-complete demo showing all mechanics; polished vertical slice; infrastructure for more | 4, 5, registries (3.2), `docs/DESIGNER.md` |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset to defaults | 4.17 |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menus; any input exits; may cheat | 4.18, 8.4, 8.7 |\n| Narrative tone like the source's | 4.12, 5.1, 5.6 |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse; prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs, Xbox option | 4.3, 4.14, 4.15, E5, E6 |\n| No dense web-style data screens | 4.14, 4.15, 5.8 |\n| Touch-only: no touch controls, the notice, the settings button, attract runs | 4.19, 8.7 |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | 6 (cut list removes whole features only) |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and an About/Credits screen | 5.8, Appendix B |\n| `exit-interview.json` in the exact shape, parsing as JSON | Appendix A (check with `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`) |\n| Headless testing, a scripted playthrough, one command printing only failures and a count | 8 |\n| Server on 127.0.0.1, port 0, confirm the page, stop only your own PIDs | 8.6 |\n| No subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit | 0 |\n\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TmzqSvesejoyb8KCMw8Trc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
