{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghuvUpcFFBGT8GkZxsrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've closed the three gaps you raised. I re-ran the suite and the two hub scenarios after the changes, and all pass.\n\n- **Full spec check:** I read the rest of `TASK.md` and walked the plan's section 9 Done checklist row by row. Every row is covered by a feature already built and tested, except the three I flagged and now tested below.\n- **Touch-only notice:** the earlier emulation still reported a fine pointer, so I forced it to report a touch-only device. The title now shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" with the engine's settings and fullscreen buttons. A tap does not start the game, and the attract mode starts after 10 seconds (screenshot `shots/touch-notice.png`).\n- **Xbox glyphs:** I tested the Settings → Button symbols switch. On the controller, the Fire, Magic, Plant, Confirm and Cancel prompts read RT, Y, LT, A and B with Xbox symbols, and R2, △, L2, ✕ and ○ with PlayStation symbols. The keyboard shows key names.\n- **Stubs:** I removed the empty `netDraw` function, the no-op bell and lava loops, the empty `exit()` bodies, the dead `h.push && 0` line and the empty `if` blocks in the networking and hero code. A search for empty `{ }` bodies now finds only the one deliberate `update() { return; }` on the net boot scene, which has nothing to do per frame.\n\nThe suite still passes all 969 checks, including the scripted bot playthrough to the ending, and the hub harness passes its 4-player and server scenarios on the rebuilt HTML. The rebuilt `Gauntletdown-Gauntlet-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-050250.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the run folder's root. The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections in my previous reply still stand unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_